Hello out there.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.770
Nope, we don't need a Jeep.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:37.490
Uh-uh.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:41.880
Hi.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:50.580
So it's a pile of bricks.

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:51.460
See them all the time.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:57.750
Hey, another pile of bricks and a card that says Black Scorpion Wrecking Services.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:10:59.900
What could it mean?

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:01.820
Look at that!

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:03.530
Dark!

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.190
A cool Ford.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:12.360
Yeah, it's a 55 Ford with a little work.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.410
Could be cherry.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.790
Yeah, we'd chop it, drop it, add some thrush pipes.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:16.410
It'd be great.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:19.700
Certainly have no idea what could have happened or why.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.190
Who could do this to a car out here?

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:28.260
Well, I'm no insurance adjuster, but a big truck or the neighbor kids could have...

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.100
Do you read? Both ways.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:33.360
Sergeant Vega, do you read me?

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:36.480
Hey, there's a small man in the glove box.

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.380
Help me find his torso.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:39.590
Hello? Hello, do you read me?

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:42.220
5-1-1, I read you, Sergeant Vega.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:43.390
What's your location?

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.240
I'm in the front seat, but I'm not Sergeant Vega.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:48.780
Better take this. You're head man down here.

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:52.980
Hello? This is Arturo Ramos,

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.780
professor of geology from the university.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.580
My associate and I came upon this patrol car.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.270
There has been an accident.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:03.250
I believe we're a few kilometers south of the village of San Lorenzo.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:04.740
Where's Sergeant Vega?

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:06.840
He's not here, he...

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:08.130
No one is here.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.010
The car is badly damaged.

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:11.300
But there's no blood.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:12.920
Can I run off the road?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.330
There is no road.

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.240
Didn't the police sergeant make a report after the accident?

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:19.600
The radio's working.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:20.770
No, we have heard nothing.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.310
Thank you, Professor. Leave the patrol car as it is.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.380
We should order military intelligence to send an emergency unit to San Lorenzo immediately.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:28.520
We will.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:29.880
Thank you for ordering.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.280
Your total is $554, please pull ahead to the second drive-thru window, thank you.

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:35.400
Not doing any good here, pal.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:37.880
Oh?

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:41.740
Thanks.

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.950
Well, my countrymen may like rattlesnakes in the house.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:45.970
I can do without them.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:47.160
Let's take a look.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:49.220
You lost me.

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.560
Bob, if you die, can I have your hat?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.500
You know, this would make an excellent miniature golf course.

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:14.270
Hey!

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:15.750
Look back here.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:17.590
There's a key light.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:23.200
This house is filled with Christmas trees.

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.740
10 bucks a foot?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:25.410
Jesus.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:40.390
Well, at least we know they're an advanced civilization, they've got Vic's VapoRub.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:44.570
Yeah, now you're supposed to pick it up with your forearms and leave the monastery forever.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:45.290
Heh heh heh.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:46.650
I'm walking to write paper.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:53.700
Look, baby tracks.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:57.540
What's behind the curtain?

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.510
It's a baby boy!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.130
All right, kid, start talking.

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.430
Come on, man, let's just have a baby.

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:06.190
That Bradley snake is the worst kind of them all.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.090
Let's blast it.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:10.640
Come on, fella.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.420
Hey, how'd he know his name was fella?

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.330
Uh, practice, Mr. Scott?

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:19.010
Uh, used to be Mrs. Scott.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.790
I guess so, with four brothers and two sisters.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:22.830
Wait a minute, they were older than me.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.330
What do you suppose caused this wreck?

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:25.730
That police car out there?

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.420
Could have been a bull.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.970
It was, it had to be the grandpappy.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.280
the biggest bull it ever was.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:32.400
The Schlitzmalt liquor bull.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.100
The wild-eyed beast.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:35.300
The grass-eater.

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:36.290
Yep.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:36.970
So?

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:41.940
Look, when I've already got a half a dozen questions I can't answer, I try to ignore any new ones.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.320
You think we ought to use the radio to tell them about the kid?

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:44.900
Nope.

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:47.220
We ought to get to San Lorenzo as quick as we can.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:48.550
I don't know.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.010
Not a beep out of them.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:51.740
Peep.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.800
You know, if I ever have any of my own, I think I'll feed them beans and tortillas, too.

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:57.440
Then I'll be able to get some sleep nights.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:14:58.680
I doubt it.

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:01.420
Huh?

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.400
No more beans and tortillas for that, kid.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:04.700
Wait a minute.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:12.640
I'll just leave them here on the seat of the car.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.620
What's behind this tree? It's a dead cat!

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:19.860
That's right, Bob. It's a 1953 Signora Policia,

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:23.820
complete with 38 snub-nosed revolver, dilated pupils, and rigor mortis.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.780
You, too, will sleep soundly in your own Signora Policia.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:29.860
From Spiegel Catalog, Chicago, Illinois, 6060.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.240
9.

